8.
When committing code, the code must be unit, component and function tested.
When committing code, the whole team must approve the commit ( peer review ).
When committing code, the code must be documented within reason.
when beginning feature work, the team and product owner must have consensus on what will be delivered.
When closing a feature, the product owner must have reviewed it and accepted the work.

9.
The principle of daily is: what have I done, what do I plan to do today, any impediments/blockers. If the person does not do that, then structure of the daily should change.
The idea of daily is to share with your team the work you are doing so that everyone knows what is being contributed to the sprint goal.

